meta {
  name: DreamHomes Haven — Kafka canary
  type: collection
}

docs {
  # Kafka canary — proves the outbox → producer → broker → consumer pipeline

  Run this **before** the full seed to confirm Kafka is working end-to-end
  in prod. If the final notification check is green, you can seed with
  confidence. If it's red, fix Kafka first (otherwise the seeded inspections
  and offers will silently fail to deliver notifications).

  ## What it exercises

  1. Registers two throwaway users (owner + applicant).
  2. Owner creates a property + listing.
  3. Applicant submits an offer on the listing — **this is the
     `offer.submitted.v1` Kafka event**. The outbox row is written in the
     same transaction as the offer insert.
  4. Brief wait (5s) so the `OutboxRelay` background poll picks the row up,
     ships it to Kafka, and the `OfferSubmittedListener` consumer writes a
     notification row for the owner.
  5. Owner hits `GET /api/notifications/mine` — asserts an OFFER_SUBMITTED
     notification exists.

  ## How to run

  GUI:
    File → Open Collection → audit/bruno/KafkaCanary
    Pick environment: `Local` or `Prod`
    Right-click the folder → Run Folder
    Watch all 8 requests pass; the last one is the green-light signal.

  CLI:
    cd audit/bruno
    bru run KafkaCanary --env Prod

  ## What it doesn't cover

  - Inspection-requested topic (same pipeline; if offers work, inspections
    almost certainly do — the only difference is which `@KafkaListener` fires).
  - DLT routing on failure.
  - SSE notification stream.

  ## Cleanup

  Two throwaway users + one listing land in prod after this run. They use
  `kafka-canary-*@demo.dreamhomes.local` emails so they're easy to spot.
  Drop them manually (or via an admin DELETE flow) when convenient.
}
